946:
(a) The duties of the board shall be to:
(1) Promote public interest in the general improvement of the environment of Macon-Bibb County;
(2) Initiate, plan, direct and coordinate programs for litter control for the community on a sustainable basis;
(3) Implement and maintain the clean community system;
(4) Study, investigate and develop plans for improving the health, sanitation, safety, and cleanliness of Macon-Bibb County by beautifying the streets, highways, alleys, river and stream banks, lots, yards and other similar places in Macon-Bibb County;
(5) Aid in the prevention of fires, diseases and other casualties by the removal and elimination of trash and other debris from the streets, highways, alleys, lots, yards, plots and other similar places;
(6) Encourage the placing, planting and preservation of trees, flowers, plants, shrubbery and other objects or ornamentation in Macon-Bibb County;
(7) Protect song birds and other wild fowl;
(8) Advise and recommend plans to other agencies of Macon-Bibb County for the beautification of Macon-Bibb County; and
(9) Promote public interest in the general improvement of the environment of Macon-Bibb County.
(b) Nothing in this division shall be construed to abridge or change the powers and duties of other commissions, departments, boards and like agencies of Macon-Bibb County.
(O-20-0006, § 3, 1-21-2020)

947:
In order to perform the foregoing duties, the board shall have the authority to:
